  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Starting Play**: The player to the dealer's right leads the first trick with any card. 2. **Following Suit**: Players must follow the suit of the led card if able. If unable, any card may be played. 3. **Winning a Trick**: The highest card of the led suit wins the trick. No trump suit exists. 4. **Next Lead**: The winner of the trick leads the next trick with any card. 5. **Final Trick**: After 5 or 6 tricks (depending on variant), the winner of the last trick wins the game. 6. **Round Completion**: After each complete game, the deal passes to the next player clockwise.",
    Player: "1. **Starting Play**: The player to the dealer's right leads the first trick with any card. 2. **Following Suit**: Players must follow the suit of the led card if able. If unable, any card may be played. 3. **Winning a Trick**: The highest card of the led suit wins the trick. No trump suit exists. 4. **Next Lead**: The winner of the trick leads the next trick with any card. 5. **Final Trick**: After 5 or 6 tricks (depending on variant), the winner of the last trick wins the game. 6. **Round Completion**: After each complete game, the deal passes to the next player clockwise.",
    objective: 'Win the final (5th or 6th) trick. Winning earlier tricks may be disadvantageous as the trick winner must lead the next trick.',
    gameplay: "1. **Starting Play**: The player to the dealer's right leads the first trick with any card. 2. **Following Suit**: Players must follow the suit of the led card if able. If unable, any card may be played. 3. **Winning a Trick**: The highest card of the led suit wins the trick. No trump suit exists. 4. **Next Lead**: The winner of the trick leads the next trick with any card. 5. **Final Trick**: After 5 or 6 tricks (depending on variant), the winner of the last trick wins the game. 6. **Round Completion**: After each complete game, the deal passes to the next player clockwise.",
    keyRules: [
      'Card rank order (high to low): Ace, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3 (except Spades: 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3 only; no Ace of Spades).',
      'Must follow suit if able; otherwise, play any card.',
      'Only the final trick matters; earlier trick wins are often strategic disadvantages.',
      'No trump suit in standard play.',
      'Trick winner leads the next trick, forcing them to potentially give away control.',
